/-!
# Tate's determinant formula for power series quotients

Let `f₁, …, fₙ ∈ 𝒪⟦X₁, …, Xₙ⟧`, as many relations as variables, with `f = g • X` for an
`n × n` matrix `g` over `𝒪⟦X₁, …, Xₙ⟧`. When `𝒪` is Noetherian and
`T = 𝒪⟦X⟧ ⧸ (f)` is finite free over `𝒪`, the annihilator of the augmentation ideal of `T` is
generated by the class of `det g`, and its image in `𝒪` is generated by `det g(0)`. Over a field
`k` with `k⟦X⟧ ⧸ (f)` finite-dimensional, the class of `det g` lies in every nonzero ideal, and a
linear form makes the multiplication pairing perfect.

The proofs reduce to `Ideal.colon_span_eq_sup_span_det_of_isWeaklyRegular`, using a weakly
regular sequence of characteristic polynomials (resp. powers of the variables) inside `(f)`.

## References

* B. de Smit, K. Rubin and R. Schoof, *Criteria for complete intersections*, in *Modular Forms and
  Fermat's Last Theorem*, Springer, 1997, pp. 343–355, Section 2.
* J. Tate, *Homology of Noetherian rings and local rings*, Illinois J. Math. 1 (1957), 14–27.
-/

universe u v w x

